a court in belarus has handed down an  18-year prison sentence to opposition  figure sergey tekonovsky according to  state media sergey is the husband of  svetlana ticonovskaya who took over as a  presidential candidate in his place  the former video blogger had attempted  to run for president against alexander  lukashenko in the august 2020 elections  but was arrested before the vote today a  court sentenced him on charges of  organizing mass unrest in a video  message ahead of the verdict his wife  svetlana who is currently in exile in  brussels said she expected her husband  would be given a lengthy sentence and  she vowed to keep fighting for him  i will continue to defend the person i  love and who has become a leader for  millions of belarusians  i will try to do something very  difficult maybe impossible to bring  closer the moment when we will see each  other in a new belarus  so let's get straight across to a kiev  and correspondent nick connolly hi nick  what more can you tell us about this  story  well the extraordinary thing about this  case that's been at the center of  attention in belarus for months now is  that it has been going on behind closed  doors in that jail in the regionality of  gomer only about 200 km why i'm here in  ukraine's capital kiev not even the  relatives being able to really find out  what's going on there and lawyers have  been  thrown out indeed sere tiranovsky's  lawyer for most of the case was  had her legal license removed during the  case you had to change lawyers so it's  basically a very difficult situation  where very little has come out but i  think this is really important because  the regime is making clear that it is  not in any move compromise we had a  10-year sentence familiar media  calisthenics and other  prominent opposition figures so this  18-year  sentence is really an attempt to  raise the stakes maybe as some kind of  diplomatic kind of pawn maybe these  people will be their freedom will be  exchanged some 